{"name":"Blue Period","hex":"#075158","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"period","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A length of time. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A length of time in history seen as a single coherent entity; an epoch, era."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Designating anything from a given historical era.","Evoking, or appropriate for, a particular historical period, especially through the use of elaborate costumes and scenery."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/period"}],"entries":[{"title":"Picasso's Blue Period","blocks":[{"text":"The Blue Period comprises the works produced by Spanish painter Pablo Picasso between 1901 and 1904. During this time, Picasso painted essentially monochromatic paintings in shades of blue and blue-green, only occasionally warmed by other colors. These sombre works, inspired by Spain and painted in Barcelona and Paris, are now some of his most popular works, although he had difficulty selling them at the time."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/11/La_Vie_by_Pablo_Picasso.jpg/330px-La_Vie_by_Pablo_Picasso.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Picasso's_Blue_Period","wikidata":"Q1205085"},{"title":"Blue Period (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Period is the third studio album by jazz musician Miles Davis. It was released in 1953 as a 10\" LP, his second released by Prestige Records, recorded over the course of two 1951 recording sessions at New York's Apex Studio."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2f/Blue_Period_%28Miles_Davis_album_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Period_(album)","wikidata":"Q1102328"},{"title":"Blue Period (manga)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Period  is a Japanese manga series written and illustrated by Tsubasa Yamaguchi. The series has been serialized in Kodansha's seinen manga magazine Monthly Afternoon since June 2017, with its chapters collected in 19 tankōbon volumes as of May 2026. The series is licensed in English by Kodansha USA. An anime television series adaptation produced by Seven Arcs aired from October to December 2021. A live-action film adaptation premiered in Japanese theaters in August 2024."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/89/Blue_Period_Volume_1_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Period_(manga)","wikidata":"Q74458180"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/97/The_Blue_Room.jpeg/500px-The_Blue_Room.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/97/The_Blue_Room.jpeg/960px-The_Blue_Room.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/97/The_Blue_Room.jpeg/500px-The_Blue_Room.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Blue_Room.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/55/Le_Gourmet.JPG/250px-Le_Gourmet.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/55/Le_Gourmet.JPG/500px-Le_Gourmet.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/55/Le_Gourmet.JPG/250px-Le_Gourmet.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALe_Gourmet.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7d/Pablo_Picasso%2C_1901%2C_Harlequin_and_his_Companion_%28Les_deux_saltimbanques%29%2C_oil_on_canvas%2C_73_x_60_cm%2C_Pushkin_Museum%2C_Moscow.jpg/250px-Pablo_Picasso%2C_1901%2C_Harlequin_and_his_Companion_%28Les_deux_saltimbanques%29%2C_oil_on_canvas%2C_73_x_60_cm%2C_Pushkin_Museum%2C_Moscow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7d/Pablo_Picasso%2C_1901%2C_Harlequin_and_his_Companion_%28Les_deux_saltimbanques%29%2C_oil_on_canvas%2C_73_x_60_cm%2C_Pushkin_Museum%2C_Moscow.jpg/500px-Pablo_Picasso%2C_1901%2C_Harlequin_and_his_Companion_%28Les_deux_saltimbanques%29%2C_oil_on_canvas%2C_73_x_60_cm%2C_Pushkin_Museum%2C_Moscow.jpg?utm_source=e